// THE CLAIMS — one per line, each with a kind and a support set.
//
// Seeded 2026-08-17 on Kevin's mark, "build the truth-bearing spine first, not
// TANK." These are not every claim in the corpus and are not meant to be. They
// are the claims THIS SESSION actually leaned on, which is the only honest way
// to start a file whose whole subject is warrant: a spine seeded from memory
// would be the exact fault it exists to catch.
//
// ADMISSION: a claim needs a kind from the six and a support set that could
// establish a claim of that kind. There is no generic kind and no fallback.
// A claim whose supports cannot establish it comes back MISFILED rather than
// being quietly downgraded — the downgrade would be a classifier deciding, and
// nothing here decides.
//
// A BROKEN SUPPORT IS NOT A FALSE CLAIM. It is "something beneath me changed;
// I no longer know whether I stand." Nothing in this file is rewritten when a
// support goes; the break is exposed and left for a hand.
//
// Run:  node tools/standing_check.js

{"id":"descent.twelve","kind":"MEASURED","says":"The descent half of the solid holds exactly twelve members.","support":[{"of":"solid","expr":"S.MEMBERS.filter(m=>S.EMBED[m.a][2]>=0&&S.EMBED[m.b][2]>=0).length","expect":12}]}

{"id":"descent.equator.empty","kind":"MEASURED","says":"The equator carries no members, so the twenty-four part 12/12 with nothing shared.","support":[{"of":"solid","expr":"S.MEMBERS.filter(m=>S.EMBED[m.a][2]===0&&S.EMBED[m.b][2]===0).length","expect":0}]}

{"id":"descent.axis","kind":"MEASURED","says":"z is the world's own vertical: of the three fourfold axes only z has one square face all falling and the other all rising.","support":[{"of":"solid","expr":"S.SQUARES.filter(q=>q.seats.every(n=>S.SEATS[n].fall)||q.seats.every(n=>!S.SEATS[n].fall)).map(q=>q.axis).sort()","expect":["z+","z-"]}]}

{"id":"descent.bowl","kind":"MEASURED","says":"The descent half is a disk, not a solid: eight seats, twelve members, five whole panes, V-E+F=1.","support":[{"of":"solid","expr":"(()=>{const z=n=>S.EMBED[n][2],V=S.NAMES.filter(n=>z(n)>=0).length,E=S.MEMBERS.filter(m=>z(m.a)>=0&&z(m.b)>=0).length,F=S.TRIANGLES.filter(t=>t.seats.every(s=>z(s)>=0)).length+S.SQUARES.filter(q=>q.seats.every(s=>z(s)>=0)).length;return [V,E,F,V-E+F];})()","expect":[8,12,5,1]}]}

{"id":"descent.twelfth.is.lens","kind":"MEASURED","says":"The twelfth member of the descent half, in the circuit table's own order, is LENS-DEEP.","support":[{"of":"solid","expr":"(()=>{const z=n=>S.EMBED[n][2],L=S.MEMBERS.filter(m=>z(m.a)>=0&&z(m.b)>=0);return [L[11].a,L[11].b].sort();})()","expect":["DEEP","LENS"]}]}

{"id":"descent.circuits.three.each","kind":"MEASURED","says":"Each of the four circuits gives the descent exactly three of its six members.","support":[{"of":"solid","expr":"(()=>{const z=n=>S.EMBED[n][2],c=[0,0,0,0];S.MEMBERS.filter(m=>z(m.a)>=0&&z(m.b)>=0).forEach(m=>c[m.circuits[0]]++);return c;})()","expect":[3,3,3,3]}]}

{"id":"runs.homeless.are.transits","kind":"DERIVED","rule":"The descent half has twelve members and eight seats. A built mechanism that is not a vertex therefore has no place to be except a member. Counted, not read.","says":"RAIN, CHANNEL, SHOAL, SOUNDING and STILLING are transits rather than places.","support":[{"of":"claim","id":"descent.twelve"},{"of":"solid","expr":"S.NAMES.filter(n=>S.EMBED[n][2]>=0).length","expect":8},{"of":"line","file":"nesi/game2d/THE_24.md","match":"RAIN, CHANNEL,"}]}

{"id":"runs.siting","kind":"INFERRED","says":"The five transits land on members 2, 4, 7, 8 and 11 of the descent — sounding, channel, rain, shoal, withdrawal.","support":[{"of":"claim","id":"runs.homeless.are.transits"},{"of":"line","file":"nesi/game2d/descent.html","match":"THE SHOAL — arrangement, never a verdict"}]}

